  "preamble": "Loss of implosion: the alveolar implosive [ɗ] becomes plain voiced [d]. Proto-Austroasiatic *ɗ (Shorto 2006; Sidwell 2024) appears as plain d in Munda, which has no implosives (Santali ᱫᱟᱜ [dak̚ʔ] 'water'), and as Old Khmer d, which later devoiced to Modern Khmer t (Old Khmer dik > ទឹក /tɨk/). Khmer /ɗ/ is also weakened to [d] in educated speech. The evidence is comparative and drawn from Wiktionary's citations of Sidwell and Shorto.",
  "phoneticEffects": "Loss of Implosion, Airstream Change",
  "languageExamples": [
